3.4.2 added code under the comment:
/* we were breaking 2/3 of everything unconditionally.
 * we still don't want anything to survive unconditionally,
 * but we need ammo to stay around longer on average.
 */


First of all, there's a base chance of losing the projectile, plus
another chance of it being saved if it's blessed.

The base chance is, for weapons whose (enchantment - erosion) is less
than two, you have a 1/(3+erosion-enchantment) chance of it surviving.
So a +0 arrow will be lost 2/3rds of the time, a -1 arrow 3/4ths of
the time, a +1 arrow 1/2 the time, and so on.

For more highly enchanted projectiles, the base chance is 1/4 of
losing it.

After that, for blessed arrows/darts/whatever, there is an extra
chance of it surviving. The formula gets a bit complicated so I just
ripped out the code and ran it a bunch of times.

